      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under nitrogen with exclusion of air and water, THF (ca. 15 mL) was degassed by three freeze–pump–thaw cycles and condensed onto (C5Me4H)3La (142 mg, 0.28 mmol), LaCl3 (38 mg, 0.15 mmol), and sodium smeared on the bottom of a sealable flask. CO2 (1 atm) was introduced and the mixture was stirred overnight. Solvent was removed in vacuo, the solids were extracted with toluene, toluene was removed in vacuo, and the residue was dissolved in minimal diethyl ether and centrifuged. Concentration at −35 °C over 1–3 weeks gave colorless X-ray quality crystals of 1 (10 mg) as the Et2O solvate. The compound was also obtained analogously from [(C5Me4H)2La]Cl2K(THF)x and excess Na.",
