      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A THF (ca. 15 mL) solution of (C5Me4H)3La (146 mg, 0.3 mmol) was degassed by three freeze–pump–thaw cycles. CO2 (1 atm) was introduced and the solution was stirred overnight. Solvent was removed in vacuo and solids were extracted with toluene; toluene was removed to leave a pale yellow solid (mixture of carboxylate products). Concentration at −26 °C over 1–3 weeks gave yellow X-ray quality crystals of 3 (41 mg, 26%). Analogous CO2 reactions of (C5Me4H)3Ln (Ln = Nd, Sm, Gd) gave pale blue (Nd) or yellow (Sm, Gd) product mixtures characterized by IR and APCI-MS.",
